1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,162
You celebrate Ram's return on Diwali,

2
00:00:02,162 --> 00:00:04,341
but do you know Bharat's untold story,

3
00:00:04,341 --> 00:00:05,660
with just one day left?

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:08,812
Bharat was about to step into the fire.

5
00:00:08,812 --> 00:00:11,120
In all our lives, there is some wait,

6
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,989
For a job, a loved one, or good days.

7
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:16,440
Bharat's wait was fourteen years,

8
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,480
when Ram left.

9
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:20,202
Bharat went to Chitrakoot to persuade Ram.

10
00:00:20,202 --> 00:00:21,251
When Ram refused,

11
00:00:21,251 --> 00:00:24,276
Bharat returned carrying his sandals on his head,

12
00:00:24,276 --> 00:00:25,510
refusing the palace.

13
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:27,986
wearing tree bark in a hut at Nandigram,

14
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:30,694
he ruled by placing the sandals on the throne.

15
00:00:30,694 --> 00:00:31,990
And he had made a vow,

16
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,310
that the moment fourteen years were up,

17
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:35,490
if you do not appear,

18
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:36,950
I will walk into the fire.

19
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:39,284
Meanwhile, after conquering Lanka,

20
00:00:39,284 --> 00:00:41,459
Ram returned in the Pushpaka Vimana,

21
00:00:41,459 --> 00:00:44,480
sending Hanuman ahead to bring the news to Bharat.

22
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,056
Hanuman saw Bharat, his emaciated body,

23
00:00:47,056 --> 00:00:48,631
matted locks on his head,

24
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,898
With eyes full of waiting, and said,

25
00:00:50,898 --> 00:00:51,780
Ram is coming.

26
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:54,048
Bharat collapsed in sheer joy,

27
00:00:54,048 --> 00:00:55,631
then embraced Hanuman.

28
00:00:55,631 --> 00:00:58,940
Bharat placed those same sandals on Ram's feet

29
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:01,742
And said, "Your kingdom, your trust,

30
00:01:01,742 --> 00:01:03,921
I return today." Valmiki writes,

31
00:01:03,921 --> 00:01:06,850
Ayodhya was adorned with flowers and flags.

32
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,083
The whole city rushed to meet Ram,

33
00:01:08,083 --> 00:01:09,880
and today we light lamps.

34
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:13,449
Imagine how often Bharat's mind must have wavered...

35
00:01:13,449 --> 00:01:15,670
yet he stood firm, and Ram returned.

36
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:18,282
Hearing Ram was returning, Bharat said,

37
00:01:18,282 --> 00:01:21,042
True human joy comes after a hundred years.

38
00:01:21,042 --> 00:01:21,940
Didn't get it?

39
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,774
Just know this, the one who stays firm,

40
00:01:24,774 --> 00:01:26,792
happiness finally finds them,

41
00:01:26,792 --> 00:01:28,740
even if it takes many years.

42
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,212
And if things are not right yet, then...

43
00:01:31,212 --> 00:01:32,780
the picture is still... Oh,

44
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,580
you already know the next line.

45
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,428
Complete it in the comments. Jai Shri Ram.

46
00:01:38,428 --> 00:01:39,350
Happy Diwali.

